<title>SWITZERLAND: TABLE-Vontobel H1 net rises 48pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Vontobel H1 net rises 48pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		 (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p>Group net</p>
<p>  after minorities	     52.1	     vs 35.1</p>
<p> Minority interests	     1.7	     vs  2.1</p>
<p> Op profit			103.6	     vs 73.3</p>
<p> Extraordinary income	   0.3	     vs  2.4</p>
<p> Extraordinary expenses	18.5	     vs  1.6</p>
<p> Taxes			     24.1	     vs 15.7</p>
<p> Cash flow			 77.9	     vs 59.8</p>
<p> Assets under management     43.1 billion   vs 30.3 billion</p>
<p>Net interest income	    13.7	     vs  7.9</p>
<p> Net fee, commission income 123.1	     vs 94.0</p>
<p> Net trading income	    45.6	     vs 38.4</p>
<p> Other ordinary income	  7.9	     vs  1.3</p>
<p> Operating expenses	    86.7	     vs 68.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Vontobel Group, parent of Bank Vontobel, said the biggest increase within operating expenses was personnel, which rose 34 percent to 24.6 million Swiss francs. It said the reasons were performance-related pay and a staff increase to 572 employees from 557.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-258 7340</p>
</text>
